Porting Cooperative Linux to x86-64 (MoCoLinux)
===============================================================================

Goal: a 64-bit coLinux whose first host target is Windows XP Professional x64
Edition, then a forward-port of the guest to a current Linux kernel.

This document is the design record for that work. It describes how the 32-bit
world switch actually works, every place it assumes 32 bits, and the order in
which to attack the problem. Read doc/building first for how the tree builds.


